A('1960-0106-camau', '1960-01-06', VH, 'Cà Mau. The provincial committee meets, Jan. 6: the armed units to be brought up to strength, and a simultaneous rising of the people to be backed.', 'II, 339', place='ca-mau', vis=True, also=['vietnam-operations'])
A('1960-0115-kienphong', '1960-01-15', VH, 'Kiến Phong. The night of Jan. 15, the people of three communes of Hồng Ngự district, Tân Thành, Thường Thới and Thường Phước, rise together. By Jan. 20 the province claims 165 of the Saigon side killed or wounded and 40 taken.', 'II, 324–25', to='1960-01-20', place='kien-phong', also=['vietnam-operations'], extra='The time is the first day\'s.', band_='night')
A('1960-0117-bentre', '1960-01-17', VH, 'Bến Tre. The rising (Đồng Khởi) begins in three communes, Định Thủy, Phước Hiệp and Bình Khánh, as the enlarged provincial committee, called by Nguyễn Thị Định Jan. 1 at Tân Huề, Mỏ Cày, had decided. Định Thủy up at 8 a.m. Jan. 17, Phước Hiệp free Jan. 19, Bình Khánh at 2 a.m. Jan. 20. By Jan. 24, 47 communes of five districts are up, 22 cleared of the Saigon administration.', 'II, 318–23', to='1960-01-24', place='ben-tre', names=['Nguyễn Thị Định'], also=['vietnam-operations', 'vietnam'], time='08:00', extra='The time is the first day\'s, Định Thủy.')
A('1960-0125-longan', '1960-01-25', VH, 'Long An. The night of Jan. 25, Platoon 231 of the province\'s Battalion 506 takes the Đức Lập post on Route 8, held by a platoon of the Civil Guard. Jan. 26 the people of seven districts rise.', 'II, 333', to='1960-01-26', place='long-an', also=['vietnam-operations'], band_='night')
A('1960-0128-longan2', '1960-01-28', VH, 'Long An. South of Route 4, the disguised Battalion 508 takes the Đông Thạnh post the night of Jan. 28 (13 weapons) and the Hưng Long post Jan. 29 (30 prisoners, 24 weapons).', 'II, 334', to='1960-01-29', place='long-an', also=['vietnam-operations'], band_='night')
A('1960-0128-kientuong', '1960-01-28', VH, 'Kiến Tường. The rising begins. Feb. 2 the provincial and district forces take the Sông Trăng post and force the withdrawal of posts and watchtowers along the road.', 'II, 334', to='1960-02-02', place='kien-tuong', also=['vietnam-operations'], check='the history gives the start (Jan. 28) and the Sông Trăng post (Feb. 2) and tallies to Mar. 2 (II, 335: 56 killed, 300 Civil Guard and Self-Defense men destroyed or dispersed, over 200 weapons, 11 communes).')
A('1960-0131-thudaumot', '1960-01-31', VH, 'Thủ Dầu Một. The provincial committee meets at Giếng Chảo, the An Điền forest, Bến Cát, Jan. 31 and decides to use all its political and armed forces for a rising Feb. 25.', 'II, 343', place='thu-dau-mot', vis=True, also=['vietnam-operations'])
A('1960-0205-cantho', '1960-02-10', VH, 'Cần Thơ. The provincial committee meets Feb. 10 and drops the sect names of its armed units; the Tây Đô Battalion formed.', 'II, 341', place='can-tho', vis=True, also=['vietnam-operations'])
A('1960-0205-cayme', '1960-02-05', VH, 'Cần Thơ. The Tây Đô Battalion ambushes a company of the Civil Guard at Cây Me, Trường Thành commune, Ô Môn, Feb. 5, to set the ground for the rising. The night of Feb. 28 it destroys the Vàm Xáng post at Nhơn Nghĩa.', 'II, 341', place='can-tho', also=['vietnam-operations'], check='Feb. 28 (the Vàm Xáng post) is a second event of the history, in the same sentence; not entered separately.')
A('1960-0212-rachgia', '1960-02-12', VH, 'Rạch Giá. The night of Feb. 12, Company 202 of the Ngô Văn Sở Battalion, with part of the provincial committee\'s guard, takes the command of a Saigon sweep and a Ranger company at Xẻo Cạn, An Biên.', 'II, 342', place='rach-gia', also=['vietnam-operations'], band_='night')
A('1960-0215-goquao', '1960-02-15', VH, 'Rạch Giá. Company 203 of the Ngô Văn Sở Battalion attacks the district seat of Gò Quao, destroying a Self-Defense post and some strongpoints within it.', 'II, 342', place='go-quao', also=['vietnam-operations'])
A('1960-0214-hatien', '1960-02-14', VH, 'Hà Tiên. The Lê Quang Battalion, 93 men with rifles and machetes, attacks three posts of the Civil Guard Feb. 14 and frees 7,000 people of the Ba Thê agroville in a night. Feb. 16 Saigon sends a paratroop battalion, a Ranger company and three Civil Guard companies against it.', 'II, 342–43', to='1960-02-16', place='ha-tien', also=['vietnam-operations'])
A('1960-0225-benCat', '1960-02-25', VH, 'Thủ Dầu Một. The rising begins the night of Feb. 25 at the points set by the province and districts. At Bến Cát the armed forces surround the Phú An and Rạch Bắp posts and set off carbide in bamboo tubes and mash jars to sound like heavy guns.', 'II, 344', place='thu-dau-mot', also=['vietnam-operations'], follows=None, band_='night')
A('1960-0306-bendua', '1960-03-06', VH, 'Cà Mau. 6:30 a.m., Mar. 6. The Ngô Văn Sở Battalion ambushes a column of a Saigon company, a Civil Guard squad and the Đầm Dơi district chief at Bến Dựa on the Cái Ngang river.', 'II, 340', place='ca-mau', time='06:30', also=['vietnam-operations'])
A('1960-0319-caygiang', '1960-03-19', VH, 'Cà Mau. The Phú Lợi Battalion, of the provincial force, attacks the Cây Giang post, destroys a platoon of the Self-Defense Corps and takes all its uniforms and supplies.', 'II, 340', place='ca-mau', also=['vietnam-operations'])
A('1960-0313-nocongtia', '1960-03-13', VH, 'Quảng Nam. The people of Nóc Ông Tía, Phước Sơn district, 11 self-defense men and 30 families, rise Mar. 13, kill a squad of the Civil Guard with machetes, burn the Saigon administration\'s office and go into the forest. Five days later a company burns the hamlet and is stopped by spiked traps. The first armed rising in the province\'s mountains.', 'II, 353–54', place='quang-nam', also=['vietnam-operations'])
A('1960-03-diem-bentre', '1960-03', 'vietnam', 'Ngô Đình Diệm goes to Bến Tre in March to see the situation and steady his troops and officials.', 'II, 336', when='Mar.', names=['Ngô Đình Diệm'], place='ben-tre', tags=['polity:rvn'], also=[], check='the day.')
A('1960-0325-bentre', '1960-03-25', VH, 'Bến Tre. About 10,000 men of mixed forces (marines, paratroops, Rangers), under Gen. Đỗ Cao Trí, sweep the three communes of Bình Khánh, Phước Hiệp and Định Thủy.', 'II, 336', place='ben-tre', names=['Đỗ Cao Trí'], also=['vietnam-operations'])
A('1960-0401-bentre2', '1960-04-01', VH, 'Bến Tre. The people of the three communes, Định Thủy, Bình Khánh and Phước Hiệp, make a "reverse evacuation" to the district town of Mỏ Cày, Apr. 1.', 'II, 337', place='ben-tre', also=['vietnam-operations'])
A('1960-0420-bentre3', '1960-04-20', VH, 'Bến Tre. The Saigon troops withdraw from Định Thủy, Bình Khánh and Phước Hiệp, Apr. 20.', 'II, 338', place='ben-tre', also=['vietnam-operations'])
A('1960-0326-cantho2', '1960-03-26', VH, 'Cần Thơ. The Tây Đô Battalion takes the post at Cờ Đỏ, Ô Môn, Mar. 26, destroying a second Civil Guard company and taking more than a ton of arms and ammunition.', 'II, 341', place='can-tho', also=['vietnam-operations'])
A('1960-0409-xeoco', '1960-04-09', VH, 'Cần Thơ. A Saigon sweep into Xẻo Cỏ, Long Phú, Apr. 9: the Tây Đô Battalion destroys 79 men, a Civil Guard province chief among them.', 'II, 341', place='can-tho', also=['vietnam-operations'])
A('1960-03-biennhoa', '1960-03', VH, 'Biên Hòa. With the provincial armed forces\' help, the people of four communes of War Zone D rise early in March: Thường Lang, Tân Tịch, Tân Hòa and Mỹ Lộc, the committee left with two cells, a platoon and four members under Lê Quang Chữ.', 'II, 348', when='Mar., early', place='war-zone-d', also=['vietnam-operations'])
A('1960-0731-baccruong', '1960-07-31', VH, 'Bình Thuận. 12:15 a.m., July 31. Unit 2/9, the provincial armed force, with Tánh Linh district\'s three men and 100 porters, attacks the district seat of Hoài Đức at Bắc Ruộng to break the concentration area and take the people to the base. The unit had been sent off at 2 p.m. July 30.', 'II, 372–73', place='bac-ruong', time='00:15', also=['vietnam-operations'], extra='Time: 0:15, July 31.')
A('1960-0814-phuyen', '1960-08-14', VH, 'Phú Yên. The provincial Party congress, the first of the war: held Aug. 14.', 'II, 380', place='phu-yen', vis=True, check='where in the province.')
A('1960-0829-ninhthuan', '1960-08-29', VH, 'Ninh Thuận. The night of Aug. 29–30, part of the Interprovince 3 armed forces under Phan Văn Hược, with Vũ Tấn Hạt and Bùi Đức Thành, attacks the posts of Tà Lú and Ma Ty.', 'II, 374', to='1960-08-30', place='ninh-thuan', names=['Phan Văn Hược', 'Vũ Tấn Hạt', 'Bùi Đức Thành'], also=['vietnam-operations'], band_='night')
A('1960-0902-binhdinh', '1960-09-02', VH, 'Bình Định. Unit 2/9, the province\'s first concentrated armed unit, 35 men, formed Sept. 2 at Tu Cơ Rông, Vĩnh Thạnh.', 'II, 379', place='binh-dinh', vis=True, also=['vietnam-operations'])
A('1960-0923-hoaitan', '1960-09-23', VH, 'Bình Định. Unit 2/9 makes its first attack, on the Saigon office of Hoài Tân commune, Hoài Nhơn, held by a platoon of the Self-Defense Corps. The same night the province\'s sappers with Hoài Ân district\'s armed squad take the Ân Nghĩa commune office: a platoon taken, 25 weapons.', 'II, 379', place='binh-dinh', also=['vietnam-operations'], band_='night')
A('1960-0914-westnambo', '1960-09-14', VH, 'Western Nam Bộ. By the Regional Committee\'s order of its fifth conference, the Western interprovince committee sets the rising for Sept. 14. Cà Mau, Rạch Giá, Cần Thơ, Sóc Trăng, Trà Vinh and Vĩnh Long rise that night and the next days.', 'II, 357–63', to='1960-09-16', place='ca-mau', vis=True, also=['vietnam-operations'], check='the day.', band_='night')
A('1960-0914-camau2', '1960-09-14', VH, 'Cà Mau. The U Minh Battalion starts the rising Sept. 14 by an attack on the district seat at Sông Ông Đốc. By December the province had razed 62 posts, taken over 3,000 weapons and cleared 55 of 65 communes and 500 of 550 hamlets.', 'II, 357–58', place='song-ong-doc', also=['vietnam-operations'])
A('1960-0914-rachgia2', '1960-09-14', VH, 'Rạch Giá. The night of Sept. 14, the U Minh 101 Battalion surrounds and attacks the posts of Trà Quớn and others. By early October the province had destroyed or forced out 500 posts and cleared 15 communes and 350 hamlets.', 'II, 358–59', place='rach-gia', also=['vietnam-operations'], band_='night')
A('1960-0915-socTrang', '1960-09-13', VH, 'Sóc Trăng. At 7 p.m. Sept. 13 guerrillas and people besiege the Bến Bạ post at An Thạnh Nhì, Long Phú, with loudspeakers and soldiers\' families. The post falls at dawn Sept. 15.', 'II, 360', to='1960-09-15', place='soc-trang', also=['vietnam-operations'], time='19:00', extra='The time is the first day\'s.')
A('1960-0914-travinh', '1960-09-14', VH, 'Trà Vinh. The rising begins Sept. 14 in three communes: Mỹ Long, Hiệp Mỹ and Hiệp Thạnh. At 6 p.m. Sept. 15 the post at Hiệp Thạnh surrenders; the Hiệp Mỹ post is abandoned that night. Sept. 15, 12,000 from nearby communes and 2,000 townspeople march in the provincial town against terror.', 'II, 361', to='1960-09-16', place='tra-vinh', also=['vietnam-operations'], tags=['ok:fields-time'])
A('1960-0914-vinhlong', '1960-09-14', VH, 'Vĩnh Long. The rising begins Sept. 14 with attacks on the posts at Giồng Nổi and Tâm Vu. Sept. 15 over 10,000 people march from the countryside to the province chief\'s residence with a petition.', 'II, 362–63', to='1960-09-15', place='vinh-long', also=['vietnam-operations'])
A('1960-0920-travinh2', '1960-09-20', VH, 'Trà Vinh. On the Khmer festival of Đônta over 20,000 Khmer and 2,000 monks go into the provincial town for their rights and against terror.', 'II, 362', place='tra-vinh', also=['vietnam-operations'])
A('1960-1004-travinh3', '1960-10-04', VH, 'Trà Vinh. A larger march in the provincial town, Oct. 4: 40,000 from the countryside and 5,000 townspeople against sweeps and conscription, for a new administration.', 'II, 362', place='tra-vinh', also=['vietnam-operations'])
A('1960-0923-midnambo', '1960-09-23', VH, 'Central Nam Bộ. The interprovince committee sets Sept. 23 for the rising of all its provinces. Mỹ Tho\'s order goes out that day.', 'II, 363, 368', place='ben-tre', vis=True, also=['vietnam-operations'])
A('1960-0924-bentre4', '1960-09-24', VH, 'Bến Tre. Sept. 21–22 the province feints with tens of thousands of people; Sept. 24, 5 p.m., drums and clappers sound everywhere and that night the people of nearly 100 communes demonstrate and besiege posts. Mỹ Tho\'s second wave begins that night.', 'II, 363–66', place='ben-tre', time='17:00', also=['vietnam-operations'], extra='The time is Sept. 24, the day the drums sounded.')
A('1960-0929-mytho', '1960-09-29', VH, 'Mỹ Tho. Over 8,000 people go to the province chief\'s residence Sept. 29 to face the Saigon side.', 'II, 367', place='my-tho', also=['vietnam-operations'])
A('1960-1015-trabong', '1960-10-15', VH, 'Quảng Ngãi. The night of Oct. 15, Unit 339 attacks the district seat of Trà Bồng.', 'II, 378', place='tra-bong', also=['vietnam-operations'], band_='night')
A('1960-1023-gialai', '1960-10-23', VH, 'Gia Lai. Oct. 23 the province\'s armed forces take the Can Nác post and then the Lệ Thanh settlement, backing the risings in districts 4 and 5 that join the freed Kon Tum country.', 'II, 376', place='gia-lai', also=['vietnam-operations'])
A('1960-1027-daklak', '1960-10-27', VH, 'Đắk Lắk. The night of Oct. 27 the provincial forces attack the posts of Plây Lốc, Ea Nu and Ea Thu, backing the risings in the northeast and at Ban Mê Thuột.', 'II, 376', place='dak-lak', also=['vietnam-operations'], band_='night')
